    "heading": "Name the decision and the queue owner",
    "body": "In the onboarding handoff packet workflow, a client onboarding handoff arrives before anyone confirms the client, the period, or the responsible queue. The onboarding handoff packet intake note separates a new request from a correction to an earlier record. The onboarding handoff packet handoff begins with a named receiver and ends only when that receiver accepts the case in the onboarding tracker. The onboarding handoff packet decision is written in one sentence so a second reviewer can tell whether the case is finished. Review pass 1.1: the account team files the onboarding handoff packet evidence.\n\nThe onboarding handoff packet working file joins the handoff note, the milestone list, the owner, and the client context on one case reference so the decision can be rebuilt. The onboarding handoff packet queue shows the promised response time, the current owner, and the next action. A onboarding handoff packet case without a named owner is treated as unassigned, even when a document is already attached. Review pass 1.2: the account team files the onboarding handoff packet evidence."
