    "body": "The onboarding handoff packet close event is the acknowledged handoff record, confirmed in the onboarding tracker rather than inferred from a status label. When the handoff omits the client context, the dependent action stops and the conflict is logged in the onboarding tracker. The onboarding handoff packet exception log records the client impact, the stop time, and the restart time. A onboarding handoff packet close that changes handoff note keeps the prior value available for comparison. Review pass 5.1: the account team files the onboarding handoff packet evidence.\n\nFor onboarding handoff packet, the measured interval runs from the request in the handoff note to the acknowledged handoff record in the onboarding tracker. The onboarding handoff packet record is short enough to read during the day and specific enough to survive a later audit. The final onboarding handoff packet check compares the client context with the surviving value in the onboarding tracker; a status label is not a close. Review pass 5.2: the account team files the onboarding handoff packet evidence."
